            <ArticleTitle>[Possibilities of the use of various biochemical and immunologic indicators in the differential diagnosis of unstable stenocardia and acute myocardial infarction].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>21-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Changes of systemic immune status, involved in the immunopathogenesis of atherosclerosis, have been identified in patients with unstable angina pectoris. The developing acute myocardial infarction is accompanied by the formation of a myocardial aseptic inflammatory focus, from which biologically active products are absorbed, resulting in additional immunologic shifts. A differential diagnosis algorithm has been evolved on the basis of the comparison of a series of biochemical and immunologic parameters in patients with unstable angina, investigated at the peak of its clinical manifestations, and those with acute myocardial infarction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
